      "title": "M7",
      "body": "A minor triad with a minor 7th on top is an **m7** chord. Am7 is A C E G. In a major key, ii, iii and vi are m7 chords.\n\n**Why it matters:** It is the mellow minor sound of soul, funk and jazz. ii7–V7–I is the jazz turnaround with 7ths added.",
